**Command Injection Vulnerability:**

An error-based SQL injection attack occurs when an attacker can inject SQL commands into a database by exploiting the SQL syntax error, rather than the explicit malicious SQL commands. This is a fundamental aspect of most SQL injection vulnerabilities and can be executed through SQL error messages or SQL queries that can lead to unexpected or malicious SQL commands being appended to the input data.

